---
import App from '../layouts/App.astro';
import { CLAIMS, ATTACKS, txOutcome } from '../data/claims';
import { txUrl, accountUrl } from '../data/testnet';
const REPO = 'https://github.com/RoylTEE/RoylTEE/blob/main/';
const statusText = { live: 'Reading', test: 'Test only', pending: 'Pending deploy' } as const;
const attackText = { refused: 'Refused on chain', contained: 'Contained on chain', test: 'Test only', pending: 'Pending deploy' } as const;
const curl = `curl -s https://rpc.testnet.near.org -H 'content-type: application/json' \\
  -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"query","params":{"request_type":"view_access_key_list","finality":"final","account_id":"s2.reg.royltee-dev.testnet"}}'`;
---
<App area="verify" title="Verify" intro="Check the deployment yourself: every claim with its code, its test and its transaction, the code running on each contract, the share accounts with no keys, and the keys still left on the contract accounts. Everything marked live is read from testnet now, with view calls only.">
  <section class="figures kpi" data-vfig><p class="loading figure">Reading testnet</p></section>
  <section class="figures kpi" data-claims-sum><p class="loading figure">Reading claims</p></section>
  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="cl-h" id="claims">
    <div class="panel-head"><h2 id="cl-h">Every claim, checked</h2><span class="caption">Claim, code, test, evidence</span></div>
    <ul class="proofs">
      {CLAIMS.map((c) => (
        <li class="proof" data-claim={c.id} data-check={c.check ?? ''} data-status={c.status}>
          <div class="proof-top">
            <p class="proof-claim">{c.claim}</p>
            <div class="proof-result" data-result><span class={`badge ${c.status === 'pending' ? 'warn' : c.status === 'test' ? 'plain' : 'info'}`}>{statusText[c.status]}</span><div class="caption" data-detail></div></div>
          </div>
          {c.note && <p class="caption">{c.note}</p>}
          <dl class="proof-grid">
            <div><dt>Code</dt><dd>{c.code.map((r) => <div><a class="link mono hash" href={`${REPO}${r.file}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{r.file.split('/').pop()}</a> <span class="mono hash">{r.fn}</span></div>)}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Tests</dt><dd>{c.tests.length ? c.tests.map((t) => <div class="mono hash">{t}</div>) : <span class="caption">none until deployed</span>}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>On-chain evidence</dt><dd>{c.evidence.length ? c.evidence.map((e) => (
              'tx' in e
                ? <div><a class="acct-link" href={txUrl(e.tx)} target="_blank" rel="noopener" title={txOutcome(e.tx)}>{e.tx.slice(0, 8)}</a> <span class="caption">{e.what} ({txOutcome(e.tx)})</span></div>
                : <div><a class="acct-link" href={accountUrl(e.account)} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{e.account}</a> <span class="caption">{e.what}</span></div>
            )) : <span class="caption">Pending deploy</span>}</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="panel-foot">Live checks use read-only view calls to a public testnet node. A pass means the chain matches the claim now. The test names are in contracts/ and site/tests; the repository test <span class="mono">tests/claims.test.ts</span> fails if a name here does not exist. Rows marked Pending deploy have nothing on chain yet and are not counted as passing.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="br-h" id="break">
    <div class="panel-head"><h2 id="br-h">Try to break it</h2><span class="caption">Attack, what the contract does, proof</span></div>
    <ul class="proofs">
      {ATTACKS.map((a) => (
        <li class="proof" data-attack={a.id}>
          <div class="proof-top">
            <p class="proof-claim">{a.attack}</p>
            <div class="proof-result">{a.tx && <a class="acct-link" href={txUrl(a.tx)} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{a.tx.slice(0, 8)}</a>} <span class={`badge ${a.status === 'refused' ? 'ok' : a.status === 'pending' ? 'warn' : a.status === 'contained' ? 'info' : 'plain'}`}>{attackText[a.status]}</span></div>
          </div>
          <p class="proof-does">{a.result}</p>
          {a.note && <p class="caption">{a.note}</p>}
          <p class="caption">Test: {a.tests.length ? a.tests.map((t, i) => <><span class="mono hash">{t}</span>{i < a.tests.length - 1 ? ', ' : ''}</>) : 'none until deployed'}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="panel-foot">Where a row says Test only, no transaction exists: the refusal was proven in the sandbox, not on testnet. Open the linked transactions to read the contract's own error text.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="ch-h">
    <div class="panel-head"><h2 id="ch-h">Contract code</h2><span class="caption">Code hash on chain now against the deploy record</span></div>
    <div class="table-wrap" data-code><p class="loading panel-body">Reading code hashes</p></div>
    <p class="panel-foot">The deploy record is deployments/testnet.json in the repository. The wasm files are built locally and not committed. A fresh build of the current source with scripts/build-wasm.sh gives the sha256 of the deployed registry and of the vault code it deploys; that was checked on one machine, so other machines are UNVERIFIED. The Mock USDC on chain is an older build that a fresh build does not reproduce. Share accounts s1 to s7 keep the vault code of the first registry deploy, listed as an earlier build. The first deployed registry wasm is kept in the repository as a test fixture for the upgrade test.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="sa-h">
    <div class="panel-head"><h2 id="sa-h">Share accounts</h2><span class="caption">Vault code and access keys of every share account</span></div>
    <div class="table-wrap" data-vaults><p class="loading panel-body">Reading share accounts</p></div>
  </section>
  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="k-h">
    <div class="panel-head"><h2 id="k-h">Keys still on contract accounts</h2></div>
    <div class="table-wrap" data-keys><p class="loading panel-body">Reading keys</p></div>
    <p class="panel-foot">The registry and the Mock USDC contract each keep one full access key; both registry updates were deployed in place with it. Deleting them is planned after that update (roadmap), once the code is final. Until then the registry itself is not keyless; the share accounts are.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="cmd-h">
    <div class="panel-head"><h2 id="cmd-h">From your own machine</h2><span class="caption">No wallet needed</span></div>
    <div class="panel-body">
      <p class="small">From a clone of the repository, this checks all 13 share accounts, the code hashes and the balances against the deploy record:</p>
      <pre class="code"><code>npm run verify:testnet</code></pre>
      <p class="small">Or ask a public testnet node for the keys of the share account that was sold. The answer is an empty list:</p>
      <pre class="code"><code>{curl}</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>
</App>
<script>import '../scripts/verify.ts';</script>
<style is:global>
  .code { margin: 0; padding: var(--s4); background: var(--ink); color: #f3f1ea; border-radius: var(--r-ctl); overflow-x: auto; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: var(--fs-12); line-height: 1.6; }
  .hash { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: var(--fs-12); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .proofs { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .proof { padding: var(--s4) var(--s5); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); display: grid; gap: var(--s2); }
  .proof:first-child { border-top: 0; }
  .proof-top { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--s4); align-items: flex-start; }
  .proof-claim { margin: 0; font-weight: 500; }
  .proof-result { flex: 0 0 15rem; text-align: right; }
  .proof-does { margin: 0; }
  .proof-grid { margin: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.2fr 1.6fr; gap: var(--s4); }
  .proof-grid dt { font-size: var(--fs-12); color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; margin-bottom: var(--s1); }
  .proof-grid dd { margin: 0; display: grid; gap: var(--s1); }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .proof-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .proof-top { flex-direction: column; } .proof-result { flex: none; text-align: left; } }
</style>
